event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":87,"item_id":"rs_033fedc7c1178dd3016acb4a4ee4048196ac41f151c0b71f6d","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Updating count queries**\n\nI need to update the existing brittle count. It looks like I should implement select queries to replace all instances via exact entries, maybe three? I'm running into issues since oldText is nonunique, and I can't use the tool for global replacement as bash disallows those edits. I want to ensure precision, so I'll have to use distinct enclosing lines to manage this effectively. There's a lot to consider in this process!"}

